                        ],
                        "form": "ataraxieën"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7c7af6f5-7c8f-37db-b335-a29a427a0937",
                        "entry_id": "91f2dbfc-306a-39f9-831e-b5fe83c89e36",
                        "glosses": [
                            "onverstoorbare staat die zich kenmerkt door vrijheid van zorgen, affectieloosheid en emotionele gelatenheid"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "abcbd312-40b6-4293-b8fd-06aa9f0c1683",
                        "source_entry_id": "91f2dbfc-306a-39f9-831e-b5fe83c89e36",
                        "source_sense_id": "7c7af6f5-7c8f-37db-b335-a29a427a0937",
                        "source_sense_description": "onverstoorbare staat die zich kenmerkt door vrijheid van zorgen, affectieloosheid en emotionele gelatenheid",
                        "target_lang_word": "ataraxy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ataraxy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a144d542-33b1-30e1-a2bd-acd28f2db04d",
                                        "entry_id": "5cd06b98-075a-3e8c-950e-3d4bfb724978",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ataraxia; freedom from mental disturbance; imperturbability, dogged indifference."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c9747ecf-a2b2-4aa1-8a01-25ac347441fd",
                                                "sense_id": "a144d542-33b1-30e1-a2bd-acd28f2db04d",
                                                "text": "When the Pyrrhonians say, that ataraxy is the chiefe felicitie, which is the immobilitie of judgement, their meaning is not to speake it affirmatively[…]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1062844b-9948-45ca-95a4-950880285562",
                                                "sense_id": "a144d542-33b1-30e1-a2bd-acd28f2db04d",
                                                "text": "Youth all around prancing, vociferating, mocking; callow and alien youth, having to be looked after and studied and taught, as though nothing but it mattered, term after term—and now, all of a sudden, in mid-term, peace, ataraxy, a profound and leisured stillness."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78a804c7-6a03-4fb6-bc20-1a761ee880cd",
                                                "sense_id": "a144d542-33b1-30e1-a2bd-acd28f2db04d",
                                                "text": "There was no longer any need for fortitude: he felt nothing at present and there was no point in artificial ataraxy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8abb3f7e-e5fd-4d66-8d2c-07f8ac3fd4c4",
                                                "sense_id": "a144d542-33b1-30e1-a2bd-acd28f2db04d",
                                                "text": "I was nonplussed, I stared at my teacher, never before had his swollen face seemed so replete with indifference, stone ataraxy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4ba3dd39-fe17-3d66-9e9c-db8806190f3d",
                                        "entry_id": "5cd06b98-075a-3e8c-950e-3d4bfb724978",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "State of psychological calm and tranquility, absence of discomfort, or metabolical inactivity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5bd70d53-d206-4155-a159-5318dc799d35",
                                                "sense_id": "4ba3dd39-fe17-3d66-9e9c-db8806190f3d",
                                                "text": "Ataraxy can be produced by ataractics, drugs that have a calming or quieting effect."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6252aff9-f962-45de-a81b-dc49995e05f7",
                        "source_entry_id": "91f2dbfc-306a-39f9-831e-b5fe83c89e36",
                        "source_sense_id": "7c7af6f5-7c8f-37db-b335-a29a427a0937",
                        "source_sense_description": "onverstoorbare staat die zich kenmerkt door vrijheid van zorgen, affectieloosheid en emotionele gelatenheid",
                        "target_lang_word": "ataraxia",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ataraxia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fb6660fe-555a-3924-9f82-5f6d12bbc558",
                                        "entry_id": "780d4a7b-a339-3f7e-adf3-1bc63b1400da",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Tranquility of mind; absence of mental disturbance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Greek",
                                            "literary",
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "56b0da63-fe07-45cf-8f7e-fbc12d91dc04",
                                                "sense_id": "fb6660fe-555a-3924-9f82-5f6d12bbc558",
                                                "text": "And what happineſs is there in a ſtorm of paſſions? On this account the Scepticks affected an indifferent æquipondious neutrality as the only means to their Ataraxia, and freedom from paßionate diſturbances."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6d50dbdd-71a3-4d9a-ad8d-01c6a2fb9f19",
                                                "sense_id": "fb6660fe-555a-3924-9f82-5f6d12bbc558",
                                                "text": "O, for that apathy of soul, that sweet ataraxia, of which I have heard, which forbids alike the approaches of pleasure and pain, hope and despair!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "13c88d35-984c-46ce-aefe-6efc390d923e",
                                                "sense_id": "fb6660fe-555a-3924-9f82-5f6d12bbc558",
                                                "text": "That terrible Latin poet Lucretius, whose apparent serenity and Epicurean ataraxia conceal so much despair, said that piety consists in the power to contemplate all things with a serene soul—pacata posse mente omnia tueri."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c903d0b3-0a95-4eda-8df7-f88718e5d3c0",
                                                "sense_id": "fb6660fe-555a-3924-9f82-5f6d12bbc558",
                                                "text": "[…] he was an Epicurean not in the commonly misunderstood sense, as a seeker after luxury, but in the true meaning, as a pursuer of what the Greeks call ataraxia, or freedom from disturbance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1916b3c1-27b8-4df7-bb0c-7b16b87e1c21",
                                                "sense_id": "fb6660fe-555a-3924-9f82-5f6d12bbc558",
                                                "text": "Once they’d seen that the world is nothing but atoms and void, and that we simply disintegrate after death, and so have no need to fear the Torments of Hell, they would be in a better position to cultivate ataraxia—the Greek word for the calm, unruffled composure that was the Epicurean ideal."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
